    <description>Quick Action screen flow on Opportunity (BRD ALF-RS-06 / LFRDN-336). Blocks with a message if the Opportunity already has a Quote (only one quotation per Opportunity - use the existing one to review/reissue). Otherwise lets a Sales Rep pick Quote Type (Customer/Bank Quotation), creates the Quote header, bulk-copies eligible Opportunity Line Items (Vehicle/Accessory/Package/Tint/Customization) across as Quote Line Items in one bulkified create, and auto-adds a negative Trade-In Deduction line if an Approved+Accepted Appraisal exists on the Opportunity. AF_FL_QuoteLineItem_SyncVINDisplay and AF_FL_Vehicle_SyncVINOnRestock handle VIN suppression/population/reissue automatically once lines exist - no separate VIN-required flag needed on this screen (BRD AC1/AC2/FR2 are satisfied by that automatic behavior alone). Real gap found and fixed 2026-09-08 during ALF-RS-04 full-persona-cycle testing: Get_Approved_Appraisal previously only checked AF_ApprovalStatus__c=Approved, but AF_VR_QLI_TradeInDeductionGate (LFRDN-630, pre-existing in the org) requires the linked Trade-In to ALSO have AF_TradeInOutcome__c=Accepted before a Trade-In Deduction line can be created - Approved alone throws FIELD_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_EXCEPTION and blocks the whole Create_TradeIn_Deduction_Line step (and, since it&apos;s not the terminal step, the flow&apos;s success screen never displays even though the Quote and other lines were already committed). AF_TradeInOutcome__c is a separate, later &quot;rep-recorded outcome&quot; step performed by the initiating rep after Used Car Team approval (see AF_FL_Appraisal_ApprovalApproved&apos;s own notification text: &quot;Record the customer outcome and continue with the quotation&quot;). Added AF_TradeInOutcome__c=Accepted to the same filter - mirrors the identical fix already applied to AF_FL_Appraisal_RetroAddTradeInToQuote (the reverse-sequencing flow for when the Quote already exists before approval). FOURTH real gap found live in QA: Product2Id/PricebookEntryId for the Trade-In Deduction line were hardcoded to DEV-specific record Ids, which do not exist in QA (or any other org) - Ids are never portable across orgs. Fixed by looking up Product2 by ProductCode=&apos;AF-TRADEIN-DEDUCT&apos; and its active PricebookEntry on the Quote&apos;s own Pricebook2Id (same as Get_Opportunity.Pricebook2Id used to create the Quote) via Get_TradeIn_Product / Get_TradeIn_PricebookEntry, instead of hardcoded literals - org-portable, and also correctly respects an Opportunity on a non-Standard Pricebook, which the old hardcoded PricebookEntryId could never do. Identical fix already applied to AF_FL_Appraisal_RetroAddTradeInToQuote.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
